      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that if you have a type such as\n\n```\ninterface Foo extends EmbindObject\u003c\"Foo\"\u003e {\n  doSomething(): void;\n}\n```\n\nthen `const myFooClone \u003d myFoo.clone()` will result in a `myFooClone` of type `EmbindObject\u003c\"Foo\"\u003e` rather than `Foo`, and therefore `myFooClone.doSomething()` will produce a compiler error.\n\nExample playground: https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYOwLgpgTgZghgYwgAgKIFsBGoAmB5TAKwgTAB4AVZCAD0hBwGdlGwpQBzAPmQG8AoZEOQB9MAE8ADhABcyCgG5BwhABsA9iAgAKAJRyM2BgWKlKXJQF9+-UJFiIUAMXXrqdCA2aHcJkuQAiF3UAngFhZBx1AGV1dAgwAAtOPTkAN3VgHCsbBE1WZHRxYOQAXj5LZDhmYKU8kAKi4IBhDS0ywuLXADo1TR1dJSbXVv7uqNj4pJTB-iA\n\nWe discussed the possibility of removing `clone()` altogether. Would that be an option?",
